1
00:00:10,511 --> 00:00:13,222
Happy Halloween, everyone! Oh, that's great.

2
00:00:13,305 --> 00:00:15,557
Hey. Happy Halloween.

3
00:00:16,475 --> 00:00:17,851
Jan called.

4
00:00:19,019 --> 00:00:20,521
Okay.

5
00:00:21,605 --> 00:00:24,733
I know why she's calling.

6
00:00:25,275 --> 00:00:26,443
It's the end of the month,

7
00:00:26,527 --> 00:00:30,322
and I was supposed to let somebody go by the end of the month.

8
00:00:31,532 --> 00:00:34,952
And somehow I'm supposed to put on a costume and smile.

9
00:00:36,620 --> 00:00:38,497
- Okay. <i>- Jan Levinson's office.</i>

10
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:40,916
Hey, Sherry, Michael Scott returning.

11
00:00:40,999 --> 00:00:42,584
<i>Oh, she's in a meeting.</i>

12
00:00:42,668 --> 00:00:45,337
<i>She just wanted the name of the employee you let go.</i>

13
00:00:45,420 --> 00:00:47,220
Well, I'm gonna wait until the end of the day,

14
00:00:47,297 --> 00:00:49,817
because the book said it's best to wait until the end of the day.

15
00:00:49,841 --> 00:00:52,094
<i>I just need the name of who you're planning to let go.</i>

16
00:00:52,177 --> 00:00:56,598
I don't know yet. I will have to call her back.

17
00:00:57,849 --> 00:00:59,977
<i>I know she wanted the name.</i>

18
00:01:00,352 --> 00:01:02,437
<i>Okay, Sherry?</i> Yeah.

19
00:01:02,771 --> 00:01:06,858
If you were getting fired, how would you wanna be told

20
00:01:06,942 --> 00:01:10,821
so that you could still be friends with the person firing you?

21
00:01:12,030 --> 00:01:14,283
<i>Jan wants the name as soon as possible, Michael.</i>

22
00:01:14,366 --> 00:01:16,702
Thanks. I'll call her back.

23
00:01:18,620 --> 00:01:20,747
I wish I could fire Sherry.

24
00:01:21,707 --> 00:01:23,917
<i>Hey, I'm still here.</i> Okay. I'm sorry.

25
00:01:24,001 --> 00:01:25,168
<i>Yeah.</i> No.

26
00:01:25,252 --> 00:01:26,420
<i>Okay.</i> Bye.

27
00:01:26,503 --> 00:01:28,005
<i>Hanging up now.</i>

28
00:02:04,666 --> 00:02:08,295
I mean, you hear about layoffs in the news,

29
00:02:08,378 --> 00:02:12,758
but when you actually have to do it yourself, it is heavy stuff. It's...

30
00:02:13,342 --> 00:02:16,303
I mean, these are people's lives you're talking about.

31
00:02:16,720 --> 00:02:18,513
You wanted me? Yes.

32
00:02:25,729 --> 00:02:28,732
Papier-mâché? Yes. Yes.

33
00:02:30,233 --> 00:02:31,234
Um...

34
00:02:31,610 --> 00:02:34,196
Pam, I have to let somebody go today.

35
00:02:35,030 --> 00:02:37,616
This is the hardest thing I've ever had to do.

36
00:02:37,699 --> 00:02:39,576
Why did you put it off until Halloween?

37
00:02:39,660 --> 00:02:42,120
Because it's very scary stuff.

38
00:02:42,329 --> 00:02:44,581
I think it's gonna put a damper on the party a little.

39
00:02:44,665 --> 00:02:47,501
You're worried about the party? There's a man's life at stake here.

40
00:02:47,584 --> 00:02:49,294
So it's a man? No.

41
00:02:50,212 --> 00:02:52,214
Or woman. A human life.

42
00:02:52,881 --> 00:02:55,217
If you had to guess who it would be

43
00:02:55,300 --> 00:02:58,470
based on their job performance

44
00:02:58,553 --> 00:03:02,182
and who you think deserves to be fired, who would that be?

45
00:03:02,599 --> 00:03:04,559
I just answer the phone.

46
00:03:05,352 --> 00:03:08,355
And sometimes you just let it go to voicemail.

47
00:03:14,736 --> 00:03:17,322
Your costume is fantastic.

48
00:03:18,949 --> 00:03:22,327
I know. I sent away for it in July from a catalog.

49
00:03:24,121 --> 00:03:26,373
Oh, no. Don't, don't, don't, don't.

50
00:03:28,875 --> 00:03:30,001
Okay.

51
00:03:30,293 --> 00:03:34,047
Oh, man. Okay, I have to fire somebody.

52
00:03:38,635 --> 00:03:41,513
What is that? What are you supposed to be?

53
00:03:42,723 --> 00:03:44,891
I'm the three-hole punch version of Jim,

54
00:03:44,975 --> 00:03:48,520
'cause you can have me either way, plain white Jim or three-hole punch.

55
00:03:48,603 --> 00:03:51,106
- That's great. I like it. - Oh? Yeah.

56
00:03:51,189 --> 00:03:53,483
Yeah, well, look. What about me?

57
00:03:53,775 --> 00:03:55,152
What are...

58
00:03:56,236 --> 00:03:58,447
What are you? A monk?

59
00:04:00,490 --> 00:04:02,075
I'm a Sith lord.

60
00:04:04,369 --> 00:04:05,829
Oh, big deal.

61
00:04:06,079 --> 00:04:09,082
Three round pieces of paper taped to a shirt.

62
00:04:09,833 --> 00:04:11,835
This cost me $129.

63
00:04:12,669 --> 00:04:13,795
Ass.

64
00:04:18,091 --> 00:04:20,594
Hey, you guys excited about the party?

65
00:04:20,677 --> 00:04:22,262
It's gonna be fun.

66
00:04:22,345 --> 00:04:23,430
Yeah. Yes.

67
00:04:23,513 --> 00:04:27,142
Oh, and look at you. Showing your colors.

68
00:04:27,517 --> 00:04:30,353
Don't you wish you wore a dress every day. What are you implying?

69
00:04:30,437 --> 00:04:32,856
All good. Happy Halloween.

70
00:04:33,023 --> 00:04:36,067
What happened to all of those spooky decorations that we had,

71
00:04:36,151 --> 00:04:37,694
the cobwebs and such?

72
00:04:37,778 --> 00:04:40,614
Yeah, I don't know. We put them all up last night.

73
00:04:44,659 --> 00:04:47,913
Well, you know what? Go buy some more. I'll approve the overages.

74
00:04:47,996 --> 00:04:49,164
Sound good? Yeah.

75
00:04:49,247 --> 00:04:50,332
Good.

76
00:04:50,916 --> 00:04:53,919
Oh, yeah, also, about budget stuff...

77
00:04:54,211 --> 00:04:55,212
Um...

78
00:04:55,295 --> 00:04:59,090
I'm gonna need you to find, like, a full employee salary plus benefits.

79
00:04:59,174 --> 00:05:00,717
Like 50 grand.

80
00:05:01,468 --> 00:05:04,012
I'm gonna need you to find 50 grand in the numbers.

81
00:05:04,095 --> 00:05:05,847
But we don't keep two sets of books.

82
00:05:05,931 --> 00:05:08,308
Well, that's not what I'm saying. Just, you know, find it.

83
00:05:08,391 --> 00:05:10,852
Pretend that your jobs depend on it.

84
00:05:18,819 --> 00:05:21,905
Interesting take on Dorothy. I love it.

85
00:05:21,988 --> 00:05:25,534
Hey, you know what would even be better? A soccer ball and cleats.

86
00:05:25,617 --> 00:05:28,203
<i>Why is that?</i> Bend It Like Beckham.

87
00:05:28,453 --> 00:05:31,581
Oh, like the movie about the Indian girl who plays soccer?

88
00:05:31,665 --> 00:05:34,084
Yeah, that would be perfect.

89
00:05:35,252 --> 00:05:38,171
Yeah, I mean, I guess I could do that.

90
00:05:38,255 --> 00:05:40,375
It'd be funny. I don't really play soccer or anything.

91
00:05:40,423 --> 00:05:43,134
Well, I don't really have two heads. So...

92
00:05:43,218 --> 00:05:47,264
Wait, what are you again? Oh, right. Three-hole punch!

93
00:05:50,851 --> 00:05:54,145
Okay, greatest strength. Okay, okay.

94
00:05:55,063 --> 00:05:57,858
A dog-like obedience to authority. Nice.

95
00:05:58,817 --> 00:06:01,152
But that doesn't sound good. Okay, okay.

96
00:06:01,862 --> 00:06:04,447
How about the ultimate team player?

97
00:06:05,282 --> 00:06:07,284
<i>Dwight is special.</i>

98
00:06:07,659 --> 00:06:11,621
But I don't believe that his talents are being used in this office.

99
00:06:11,705 --> 00:06:14,040
So Pam and I have put his résumé

100
00:06:14,124 --> 00:06:17,168
<i>on Monster. com, Google, Craig's List.</i>

101
00:06:17,586 --> 00:06:21,756
We're really interested most in jobs that take Dwight out of state.

102
00:06:22,716 --> 00:06:24,843
Preferably Alaska or India.

103
00:06:25,093 --> 00:06:26,636
He's a gun nut.

104
00:06:28,138 --> 00:06:29,890
Sticks to his guns.

105
00:06:31,433 --> 00:06:33,059
Well, I looked through all the budgets

106
00:06:33,143 --> 00:06:34,769
and there is one department... Yes.

107
00:06:34,853 --> 00:06:36,563
That has three people... Yeah.

108
00:06:36,646 --> 00:06:38,899
Doing the work that could be done by two.

109
00:06:38,982 --> 00:06:40,483
This is great.

110
00:06:42,903 --> 00:06:43,904
Oh.

111
00:06:44,779 --> 00:06:45,864
Yeah.

112
00:06:47,157 --> 00:06:48,158
Oh.

113
00:06:48,658 --> 00:06:50,744
Who do you think it should be? Jim, definitely.

114
00:06:50,827 --> 00:06:52,245
No, Jim brings in money.

115
00:06:52,329 --> 00:06:53,955
Phyllis? No.

116
00:06:54,039 --> 00:06:57,667
Stanley, Pam, Oscar, Meredith,

117
00:06:58,376 --> 00:07:00,337
Kevin, Angela.

118
00:07:00,420 --> 00:07:02,130
It's not a popularity contest.

119
00:07:02,213 --> 00:07:05,467
Although it does make sense to fire the least popular

120
00:07:05,550 --> 00:07:08,511
because that has the least effect on morale.

121
00:07:09,471 --> 00:07:11,514
One of the warehouse guys.

122
00:07:12,182 --> 00:07:13,266
What?

123
00:07:14,351 --> 00:07:18,146
There is someone left off that list? Who? Who is he saying?

124
00:07:19,564 --> 00:07:22,359
You're right. I didn't even think of him.

125
00:07:22,567 --> 00:07:23,944
No, Michael.

126
00:07:24,027 --> 00:07:26,071
Yeah, that's actually a really good idea. No.

127
00:07:26,154 --> 00:07:29,032
No. Not me. Yeah, I could.

128
00:07:29,115 --> 00:07:32,118
Not Dwight. I'm not saying that's what he said.

129
00:07:32,202 --> 00:07:33,954
I know that's what he said.

130
00:07:34,037 --> 00:07:35,121
What?

131
00:07:36,081 --> 00:07:37,832
Tell him not Dwight.

132
00:07:37,916 --> 00:07:40,126
That is not a very nice thing to say about him.

133
00:07:40,210 --> 00:07:41,294
Tell him to stop.

134
00:07:41,378 --> 00:07:43,046
Are you kidding? Quiet, you!

135
00:07:43,129 --> 00:07:45,006
I agree. He'd land on his feet.

136
00:07:45,090 --> 00:07:46,257
Make him be quiet.

137
00:07:49,844 --> 00:07:53,056
Those aren't chips and dip. No, I made brownies.

138
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:56,685
What?

139
00:07:56,768 --> 00:08:00,522
I'm just trying to figure out why you're sabotaging things.

140
00:08:01,022 --> 00:08:04,943
I made brownies. And I made cookies. Same category.

141
00:08:07,904 --> 00:08:11,199
I'm guessing Angela's the one in the neighborhood

142
00:08:11,282 --> 00:08:15,370
who gives the trick-or-treaters some toothbrushes,

143
00:08:16,746 --> 00:08:17,956
pennies,

144
00:08:19,249 --> 00:08:22,419
walnuts... Dunder Mifflin, this is Pam.

145
00:08:24,212 --> 00:08:25,296
Yeah.

146
00:08:26,673 --> 00:08:30,802
Just one second. I will transfer you to our manager, Michael Scott.

147
00:08:33,471 --> 00:08:34,556
Wow.

148
00:08:37,267 --> 00:08:39,019
Michael Scott here.

149
00:08:39,519 --> 00:08:42,981
Yes, I am regional manager of this orifice.

150
00:08:43,648 --> 00:08:44,774
Hmm-hmm.

151
00:08:45,775 --> 00:08:48,737
Dwight Schrute is amazing.

152
00:08:49,529 --> 00:08:50,572
Yeah.

153
00:08:50,655 --> 00:08:54,784
No, he is actually the single greatest employee of his generation.

154
00:08:55,785 --> 00:08:56,786
Hmm-hmm.

155
00:08:56,953 --> 00:08:58,496
You know what? I'm gonna tell you what.

156
00:08:58,580 --> 00:09:02,625
You hire Dwight K. Schrute and he does not meet,

157
00:09:02,709 --> 00:09:07,380
nay, exceed every one of your wildest expectations,

158
00:09:07,464 --> 00:09:12,135
well, then, you can hold me, Michael Gary Scott

159
00:09:12,343 --> 00:09:15,138
personally and financially responsible.

160
00:09:15,221 --> 00:09:18,433
Okay. Okay. Okay.

161
00:09:19,142 --> 00:09:20,268
Okay.

162
00:09:26,733 --> 00:09:29,652
Stanley, could you come with me, please? No.

163
00:09:32,822 --> 00:09:35,200
As Assistant Regional Manager... To the?

164
00:09:35,283 --> 00:09:37,952
Look, I've got some bad news.

165
00:09:38,620 --> 00:09:41,790
You're fired. You need to pack up your things and go.

166
00:09:42,415 --> 00:09:46,044
I'm serious, Stanley. It's over. I'm sorry.

167
00:09:46,127 --> 00:09:47,670
"You're fired."

168
00:09:48,254 --> 00:09:50,507
Get your fingers off my phone.

169
00:09:56,262 --> 00:09:59,641
So, how did it go with Stanley? How did he take it?

170
00:09:59,724 --> 00:10:01,768
He wouldn't listen to me. Oh, come on.

171
00:10:01,851 --> 00:10:04,246
If you wanna fire him, you're gonna have to tell him yourself.

172
00:10:04,270 --> 00:10:06,272
I don't wanna fire Stanley. I never said that.

173
00:10:06,356 --> 00:10:09,150
I'm certainly not going to do it myself.

174
00:10:09,317 --> 00:10:12,529
Get those big baleful eyes staring at me.

175
00:10:12,612 --> 00:10:15,615
Yikes. Just... Okay, just...

176
00:10:17,283 --> 00:10:18,910
Cumberland Mills?

177
00:10:20,370 --> 00:10:22,622
And how did you get my résumé?

178
00:10:23,331 --> 00:10:25,667
Oh, no, no. I'm very flattered. Don't get me wrong.

179
00:10:25,750 --> 00:10:29,003
I'm just not sure that it's my official résumé

180
00:10:29,087 --> 00:10:31,422
or if it's something that maybe

181
00:10:32,006 --> 00:10:34,509
a satisfied customer posted online.

182
00:10:35,885 --> 00:10:38,888
What does it say under martial arts training?

183
00:10:39,931 --> 00:10:42,392
Oh, okay, I'm gonna have to supplement that.

184
00:10:42,475 --> 00:10:44,686
Could I have your fax number?

185
00:10:44,853 --> 00:10:48,690
Would I ever leave this company? Look, I'm all about loyalty.

186
00:10:48,982 --> 00:10:52,944
In fact, I feel like part of what I'm getting paid for here is my loyalty.

187
00:10:53,486 --> 00:10:57,448
<i>But if there were somewhere else that valued that loyalty more highly,</i>

188
00:10:57,949 --> 00:11:01,369
I'm going wherever they value loyalty the most.

189
00:11:04,497 --> 00:11:05,748
Oh, hey.

190
00:11:06,791 --> 00:11:10,170
Oh, your dress is stuck in the back. Gotta just...

191
00:11:10,253 --> 00:11:11,254
Oh.

192
00:11:14,966 --> 00:11:16,676
So you got the fax.

193
00:11:16,759 --> 00:11:19,053
So why didn't you add it to the résumé?

194
00:11:19,137 --> 00:11:22,056
What do you mean? Of course, martial arts training is relevant.

195
00:11:22,140 --> 00:11:23,266
Oh, excuse me,

196
00:11:23,349 --> 00:11:26,394
I know about a billion Asians that would beg to differ.

197
00:11:27,687 --> 00:11:30,732
Yeah, I get a little frustrated when I'm dealing with incompetence!

198
00:11:30,815 --> 00:11:32,575
Well, you know what? You can go to hell, too,

199
00:11:32,609 --> 00:11:34,861
and I will see you there burning.

200
00:11:34,944 --> 00:11:39,115
Fine. Oh, wait, so you'll let me know when you've made a decision...

201
00:11:43,411 --> 00:11:45,288
Jim is really talented.

202
00:11:45,830 --> 00:11:49,250
And he should be the one who's getting a better job offer.

203
00:11:49,334 --> 00:11:50,835
Like, for real.

204
00:11:50,919 --> 00:11:55,548
Don't take this the wrong way, but you should go for that job.

205
00:11:58,676 --> 00:11:59,844
Um...

206
00:12:01,471 --> 00:12:03,806
It's in Maryland. Yeah.

207
00:12:04,349 --> 00:12:06,142
But, I mean, look at the salary,

208
00:12:06,226 --> 00:12:10,605
and it's definitely a step up and a challenge.

209
00:12:12,982 --> 00:12:14,108
Yeah.

210
00:12:17,278 --> 00:12:19,489
Yeah. You know what, maybe...

211
00:12:21,074 --> 00:12:22,533
Maybe I will.

212
00:12:25,745 --> 00:12:26,955
Jim.

213
00:12:28,456 --> 00:12:31,334
This is called leveraging an offer.

214
00:12:32,835 --> 00:12:36,172
Michael, can I talk to you for a moment? Oh, God.

215
00:12:36,256 --> 00:12:40,468
I just thought you should know that I was just offered a job

216
00:12:40,551 --> 00:12:42,845
with better pay, better benefits,

217
00:12:42,929 --> 00:12:45,932
and a better title at Cumberland Mills.

218
00:12:46,015 --> 00:12:48,059
Fantastic. And I turned it down.

219
00:12:48,142 --> 00:12:50,520
What? That would have solved all my problems.

220
00:12:50,603 --> 00:12:54,691
Out of loyalty to this company. Oh, you idiot. Go.

221
00:12:54,774 --> 00:12:57,777
So I was hoping to be made Assistant Regional Manager officially.

222
00:12:57,860 --> 00:13:00,446
If you left, I wouldn't have to fire anybody.

223
00:13:00,530 --> 00:13:02,740
But then you wouldn't have me here. Big deal.

224
00:13:02,824 --> 00:13:05,785
Oh, it would have worked out so well. Can you get it back?

225
00:13:05,868 --> 00:13:07,954
It's in Maryland. You could call. Can you call them?

226
00:13:08,037 --> 00:13:10,748
I can't... I suppose I... No.

227
00:13:11,249 --> 00:13:13,751
They never really made me an offer anyway.

228
00:13:13,918 --> 00:13:16,879
Why are you torturing me? God.

229
00:13:19,299 --> 00:13:23,970
Honestly, I don't think Michael has the slightest clue of who he's gonna fire.

230
00:13:24,053 --> 00:13:26,931
I think he keeps hoping that someone's gonna volunteer,

231
00:13:27,015 --> 00:13:29,934
or be run over by a bus before the deadline.

232
00:13:30,852 --> 00:13:32,652
But in the end, really, what's gonna happen is

233
00:13:32,729 --> 00:13:36,316
it's gonna be the first person to give him a dirty look in the hall.

234
00:13:36,399 --> 00:13:39,319
And therein lies the true essence of his charisma.

235
00:13:41,154 --> 00:13:44,574
Can I speak to you a minute? Yes.

236
00:14:10,683 --> 00:14:13,686
Michael, I really didn't mean to... Help me.

237
00:14:14,604 --> 00:14:17,690
I'm sorry? I want you to role-play firing me.

238
00:14:17,774 --> 00:14:20,276
I want you to fire me, and I will take it.

239
00:14:20,985 --> 00:14:22,403
Oh, you want me to be you. Yes.

240
00:14:22,487 --> 00:14:24,447
Okay. I want you to be me and I will be Creed.

241
00:14:24,530 --> 00:14:26,532
Oh, are you firing Creed? No, no, no.

242
00:14:26,616 --> 00:14:30,078
That's just first thing... Came... Can't... That head...

243
00:14:30,161 --> 00:14:33,539
We should switch seats in order to... Yes, that's a good idea.

244
00:14:33,623 --> 00:14:34,957
All right?

245
00:14:35,875 --> 00:14:37,210
Excuse me.

246
00:14:42,173 --> 00:14:44,467
I'm really sorry, but I have to let you go.

247
00:14:44,550 --> 00:14:48,012
And it's purely budgetary. It's not personal...

248
00:14:49,430 --> 00:14:52,308
I'm gonna kill myself! Wow.

249
00:14:52,392 --> 00:14:55,228
I'm going to kill myself and it's your fault!

250
00:14:55,311 --> 00:14:56,896
That's an overreaction.

251
00:14:56,979 --> 00:14:59,440
Corporate is really breathing down my neck

252
00:14:59,524 --> 00:15:02,110
and they're saying this has to be done by the end of the month...

253
00:15:02,193 --> 00:15:04,529
Is this you? Are you being you? Or is this Creed?

